# ---- Build output served by API ----
src/HomeHub.Api/wwwroot/assets/
src/HomeHub.Api/wwwroot/index.html

# ---- Test / coverage ----
[Tt]est[Rr]esults/
coverage/
*.trx

# ---- Logs ----
*.log
logs/

# ---- Cached recipe images (Stage M2, meals-planning.md D5) ----
# Downloaded at import so a recipe card doesn't depend on someone else's CDN. Machine-local cache,
# content-addressed and re-fetchable, so it is not source. Deliberately NOT under wwwroot — that
# directory is the SPA build output and every deploy replaces it wholesale.
recipe-images/

# ---- Local development TLS (scripts/make-dev-certs.sh) ----
# A private CA key that can sign for any hostname, plus the server key it signs. Both are secrets in
# the plain sense — anyone holding the CA key can mint a certificate the household's phones will
# trust without warning, because those phones have been told to trust this CA. Machine-local and
# regenerable in one command, so nothing is lost by never committing them.
certs/

# ---- OS / editor ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
*.code-workspace

# The dev CA, copied into public/ so a phone can download it from the dev server itself
# (deploy/dev-https.md §3). Public by nature — it is meant to be handed to devices — but
# machine-specific, so it is not source.
#
# Matched by name anywhere rather than at one path: `npm run build` copies everything in
# `client/public/` into `src/HomeHub.Api/wwwroot/`, so pinning the rule to the source location left
# the built copy untracked-and-committable. Delete it from `public/` once the household's devices
# are set up — otherwise every production build ships a development CA to a public URL.
homehub-dev-ca.crt
